<title>INDIA: POLL-India M&amp;M 6-mth net seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-India M&amp;M 6-mth net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Utility vehicles maker Mahindra &amp; Mahindra Ltd (M&amp;M) is projected to see its net profit rising 31.1 percent to 1.2 billion rupees in the first half of 1997/98 (April-March), a Reuter poll consensus showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sales are forecast to improve 21.6 percent to 17.4 billion rupees from 14.3 billion in the first six months of 1996/97, average estimates of 18 top brokerages said.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>M&amp;M	----PAT seen up 31.1%, sales up 21.6%</p>
<p>Average		1,211.77    924.30    17,373.32  14,286.19</p>
<p>High		   1,488.00		  23,138.00</p>
<p>Low			887.00		  14,960.00</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk +91-22-265-9000</p>
